in these cave homes for thousands of years.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"for thousands of years ระบุระยะเวลาอย่างชัดเจน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["How many years have people lived in these cave homes? Thousands of years.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-noise-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"You hear a sound like thunder. What is passing over your head?\",\"A train.\",\"You hear a sound like thunder. What is passing over your head? A train.\",\"\",[\"A bus.\",\"A plane.\",\"A taxi.\",\"A train.\"],\"The sun is shining, but you think you hear thunder. Look up! A train is passing over your head!\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"ตอนแรกคิดว่าเป็นเสียงฟ้าร้อง แต่ประโยคถัดไปบอกว่ามีรถไฟผ่านเหนือหัว","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["You hear a sound like thunder. What is passing over your head? A train.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-traffic-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Where are the trains compared with the cars?\",\"Above the cars.\",\"Where are the trains compared with the cars? Above the cars.\",\"\",[\"Above the cars.\",\"Behind every car.\",\"Inside the buses.\",\"On the same road.\"],\"Some big cities build train tracks above the city streets. One of these cities is Chicago. On the ground, cars and buses start and stop in traffic. Above them, trains are moving from station to station with no traffic jams.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"Above them บอกระดับของรางแยกจากรถที่ติดบนพื้นถนน","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Where are the trains compared with the cars? Above the cars.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-loop-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Do the tracks go to other parts of the city?\",\"Yes. They go beyond the city center.\",\"Do the tracks go to other parts of the city? Yes. They go beyond the city center.\",\"\",[\"No. They only go around the center.\",\"No. They only go inside houses.\",\"No. They only go to the river.\",\"Yes. They go beyond the city center.\"],\"In Chicago, the overhead train is called the L. The tracks make a loop around the city center and then run out in all directions to the different parts of the city. The tracks are supported by massive steel columns.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"and then run out in all directions แสดงว่าไปส่วนอื่นต่อจากวงรอบ","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Do the tracks go to other parts of the city? Yes. They go beyond the city center.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-sequence-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"Which order is right?\",\"Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"Which order is right? Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"\",[\"Gate → ticket → wait.\",\"Gate → wait → ticket.\",\"Ticket → gate → wait.\",\"Wait → ticket → gate.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"อ่านลำดับ buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}],"examples":["Which order is right? Ticket → gate → wait.","Where is the house? → In Serbia."]},{"question_id":"exam-ch34-v1-reading-train-busy-assessment-transfer","content_key":"[\"sentences\",\"At busy times, how often can a train arrive?\",\"Every ten minutes.\",\"At busy times, how often can a train arrive? Every ten minutes.\",\"\",[\"Every ten days.\",\"Every ten minutes.\",\"Once a month.\",\"Once a year.\"],\"Riding the train is easy. Riders climb stairs or take an elevator from the sidewalk to the platform. They buy a ticket, go through a gate, and wait for the next train to take them where they want to go. A train ticket costs less than a taxi ride. At busy times, trains come as often as every ten minutes. At night and on weekends, they do not come as often. Some trains run all the time, day or night.\",\"\"]","pattern_key":"exam-reading","title_th":"หาหลักฐานในข้อความ","rule_th":"อ่านคำถามว่าถามใคร ที่ไหน จำนวน วิธี หรือความหมาย แล้วหาใจความที่ตอบเรื่องเดียวกันในข้อความ","clue_th":"as often as every ten minutes บอกความถี่ที่มีได้ ไม่ใช่รับรองทุกเที่ยว","caution_th":null,"contrasts":[{"label_th":"รูปแบบแรก","text":"Where? → a place"},{"label_th":"อีกตัวอย่าง","text":"How many? → a number"}